<h1>Google Ads API Integration Design & Architecture Document</h1>
<p><strong>Prepared for:</strong> Google Ads API Compliance & Token Review Team</p>
<p><strong>Access Level Requested:</strong> Basic Access (Internal Use Only)</p>

<h1>1. Executive Summary & Purpose</h1>
<p>This document details the architectural design and implementation schema for the Google Ads API integration within our internal Lead Management CRM application. The CRM is built exclusively for internal use by our training academy's admissions and counseling teams to track, organize, and assign prospective student inquiries originating from digital marketing campaigns.</p>
<p><strong>Intended Scope of Use:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Real-time Webhook Ingestion</strong>: Capturing instant lead records directly from Google Ads Lead Form extension campaigns.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Daily Reconciliation</strong>: Performing scheduled daily read-only queries to reconcile lead data and ensure no submissions were lost due to webhook delivery failures.</li>
  <li><strong>Campaign Source Mapping</strong>: Aligning incoming inquiries to the campaign metadata (ID and Name) for internal admissions statistics.</li>
</ul>

<h1>2. System Architecture Overview</h1>
<p>Our integration leverages a serverless, decoupled architecture built on Node.js and Google Cloud Functions, ensuring secure API operations, minimal surface area exposure, and reliable operations.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Component</th>
      <th>Technology / Role</th>
      <th>Security / Protocol</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>API Endpoint Router</strong></td>
      <td>Node.js Cloud Functions</td>
      <td>HTTPS (TLS 1.3), CORS, Passkey Headers</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Secure Database Store</strong></td>
      <td>Google Firestore</td>
      <td>At-Rest Encryption, Firestore Rules</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Internal Frontend Dashboard</strong></td>
      <td>Vite + React SPA</td>
      <td>Firebase JWT Authentication</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Data Sync Flows:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Real-time Webhook Ingestion</strong>: When a lead is submitted, Google Ads posts a JSON webhook payload to our secure HTTPS Cloud Function endpoint. The function parses contact fields (name, email, phone, course) and saves them to Firestore.</li>
  <li><strong>Daily Reconciliation Job (API Sync)</strong>: Once every 24-48 hours, a scheduled Cloud Function queries the Google Ads API <code>lead_form_submission_data</code> endpoint to retrieve all submissions within the timeframe. This checks for any network dropouts or failed webhook events to reconcile database records.</li>
</ul>

<h1>3. Google Ads API Services & Methods Used</h1>
<p>Our tool interacts with the Google Ads API via the official HTTPS REST interface (using API version <strong>v24</strong>). We only perform read-only requests.</p>

<h3>Endpoints Called:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Endpoint URL</strong>: <code>https://googleads.googleapis.com/v24/customers/{customer_id}/googleAds:search</code></li>
  <li><strong>HTTP Method</strong>: <code>POST</code></li>
  <li><strong>Developer Token</strong>: Supplied in <code>developer-token</code> header.</li>
  <li><strong>OAuth Authorization</strong>: Passed as <code>Bearer {access_token}</code> in <code>Authorization</code> header.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Sample Search Query (GAQL):</h3>
<pre>
SELECT
  lead_form_submission_data.id,
  lead_form_submission_data.campaign,
  lead_form_submission_data.ad_group,
  lead_form_submission_data.lead_form_submission_fields,
  lead_form_submission_data.submission_date_time
FROM lead_form_submission_data
WHERE lead_form_submission_data.submission_date_time >= 'forty_eight_hours_ago'
LIMIT 100
</pre>

<h3>Example Mock API Request:</h3>
<pre>
POST /v24/customers/5679018078/googleAds:search HTTP/1.1
Host: googleads.googleapis.com
Content-Type: application/json
developer-token: [ENCRYPTED_DEV_TOKEN]
Authorization: Bearer [OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN]

{
  "query": "SELECT campaign.id, campaign.name FROM campaign LIMIT 1"
}
</pre>

<h3>Example Mock API Response:</h3>
<pre>
{
  "results": [
    {
      "campaign": {
        "resourceName": "customers/5679018078/campaigns/129384710",
        "id": "129384710",
        "name": "Data Science Course Admissions 2026"
      }
    }
  ]
}
</pre>

<h1>4. Data Security and Encryption Policies</h1>
<p>We prioritize security to protect sensitive Google account access credentials:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Encryption Algorithm</strong>: Credentials (such as client secrets, refresh tokens, and developer tokens) are encrypted before writing to Firestore using the <strong>AES-256-CBC</strong> algorithm.</li>
  <li><strong>Keys Management</strong>: Encryption keys are derived via cryptographic SHA-256 hashing and kept inside secure, environment-isolated configurations.</li>
  <li><strong>Access Control</strong>: Google authentication data is strictly restricted to backend functions. No credentials or keys are exposed to client browsers or frontend React code.</li>
</ul>

